  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mi>A</mi></math> is a skew symmetric matrix of order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math><mi>B</mi></math> is a&nbsp;<math><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn></math> column matrix and <math><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>, then which of the following is false?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>C</mi></math> is singular",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>C</mi></math> is non singular",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>C</mi></math> is a symmetric matrix",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>C</mi></math> is a skew symmetric matrix",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math><br /><math><msup><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>C</mi></math> is skew symmetric<br /><math><mo>&#8757;</mo></math> order of <math><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>C</mi></math> is singular and symmetric also."
  }
